        "original_id": "701a9884-a4b1-514a-a8af-7a144c0f841e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Gladstone Steel\n- Places: Crater Lake, Crater Lake National Park, Oregon, United States\n- Roles: \"father of Crater Lake\"\n- Topics: creation of Crater Lake National Park, lake features\n\nFacts:\n- William Gladstone Steel was born on September 7, 1854, and died on October 21, 1934.\n- William Gladstone Steel was called the \"father of Crater Lake\" for his role in the creation of Crater Lake National Park in Oregon, United States.\n- Crater Lake is the main feature of Crater Lake National Park.\n- Crater Lake is famous for its deep blue color and water clarity.",
